From 2dbaf4cfb6ef96b9f045bbd57c551af4ccd660ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duykhanhxx03 <duykhanhxx03@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:39:32 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] hw/virtio: virtio-vsock-sock-pci, vsock with the datapath
 in QEMU

vhost-vsock-pci needs Linux's vhost-vsock. This device runs the
virtio-vsock transport inside QEMU, so it works on Windows. The host
side is a listening socket, TCP (host-port=, host-addr= default
127.0.0.1) and/or AF_UNIX (uds-path=), speaking Firecracker's hybrid
vsock protocol: "CONNECT <port>\n", answered "OK <host port>\n" once
the guest accepts, then a raw stream. With uds-path=, guest
connections to host port P go to "<uds-path>_<P>".

Also registered as virtio-vsock-uds-pci, the name of the equivalent
device on qemu-vphone's vsock-uds branch that vphone-linux's
run-vphone.sh looks for.

- 256-entry queues: the iOS virtio driver assumes page-aligned rings.
- The host advertises buf-alloc (default 4 MiB) and buffers what the
  host socket has not taken; guest-to-host credit is never capped by a
  socket buffer. Host-to-guest data respects the guest's
  buf_alloc/fwd_cnt; QEMU sends CREDIT_REQUEST when the guest's credit
  falls under a quarter of its window, and again every 200 ms while it
  is zero (iOS volunteers an update only when its window is nearly
  full).
- Host connections are shut down before close: on Windows closing the
  socket alone did not send the peer a FIN.
- VPHONE_VSOCK_DEBUG=1 logs connections and packets on stderr.
- Not migratable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/virtio/Kconfig             |    5 +
 hw/virtio/meson.build         |    1 +
 hw/virtio/virtio-vsock-sock.c | 1076 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 1082 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 hw/virtio/virtio-vsock-sock.c

